  "_doc": "KĀLA-YANTRA fixed-operation table (charter §7). The executor reads THIS FILE FROM origin/main (never from a working tree) and refuses any kind not listed or not enabled. `enabled_by` names the item an entry serves; campaign builders never edit this file; open: enablement path. FORMAT RULE: `enabled` is the FIRST key of every entry — the plan model's detectors read it. `script` is a repository-relative path; a read-only operation's script is extracted from origin/main; a production operation runs in a private worktree at the request's reviewed_commit (which must be merged). `fixed_args` are always passed; `allowed_args` are the request-arg keys that may be appended as --key value; `needs` is the capability; `requesters` are the lanes that may request the kind (default: adhikarin only); optional `cwd` (repository-relative), `python_module` (run as python -m) and `timeout_s`. `required_rows` names the checklist rows the verifier's acceptance receipt must attest true for a mutating run of that kind. Gochara authority operations (verification_job, publish_head, rollback_head) and whole-layer operations (layer_verify, layer_publish, layer_rollback) are different surfaces and never substitute for each other. Wave 4 preparation: also_needs requires every additional capability; prepared_dry_run is disabled review metadata, never an executor kind or a dry_run_passed attestation. New kinds require a real child and phase review before enablement.",
